# The custom arm fitted to the player (#385.6): its segment lengths come from the character height until the
# reach is measured (fitSource height -> reach), a controller out of reach is met by stretching the arm by at
# most MaxArmStretch (0.10 of the arm) instead of sliding the shoulder, and a hand holding a weapon drops its
# elbow (F-300). status.json, per hand (the custom arm, vr_arms_model = custom):
#   vr.body.<hand>.custom.upperLength / .forearmLength  the fitted segment lengths, units
#   vr.body.<hand>.custom.fitSource                      height | reach
#   vr.body.<hand>.custom.stretch                        0 .. 0.10, the stretch fraction in use
#   vr.body.<hand>.custom.error                          PROPOSED: wrist to controller, units (like vr.body.<hand>.error)
#   vr.body.<hand>.custom.elbowDrop                      PROPOSED unit: elbow height below the no-weapon elbow, units (0 = none)
# The pose numbers (metres from the rig, vr-sim hand pos) are a first guess: if the arm's real reach makes
# "just past reach" miss, move the POSE - never the assertions.
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 arm-fit
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence arm-fit -Save mvp-items
@sim idle
@save mvp-items
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
# The custom arms: a test-only model since #466 (classic is the default) until #486 removes it
arms custom
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.active eq true
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq custom
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@assert vr.body.left.posed eq true

# 1. The fit: lengths set, in the Arx ratio (27.6 : 30.5), from the height until the reach is measured
@assert vr.body.right.custom.upperLength gt 10
@assert vr.body.right.custom.forearmLength gt 10
@remember upperLen vr.body.right.custom.upperLength
@assert vr.body.right.custom.forearmLength gt {upperLen}
@assert vr.body.right.custom.fitSource eq height
@assert vr.body.left.custom.fitSource eq height
@assert vr.body.right.custom.stretch eq 0

# 2. A hand far out of reach: the arm stretches, but by at most MaxArmStretch (0.10); the shoulder does not slide
vr-sim head rot 0 0 0
vr-sim hand left off
@remember shoulderY0 vr.body.right.shoulder.y
vr-sim hand right pos 0.2 -0.3 -1.5
vr-sim hand right rot 0 0 0
@frames 20
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@assert vr.body.right.custom.stretch gt 0
@assert vr.body.right.custom.stretch le 0.1
@assert vr.body.right.shoulder.y gt {shoulderY0-1}
@assert vr.body.right.shoulder.y lt {shoulderY0+1}
@shot fit-far

# 3. A hand just past the reach (z -0.535: measured in 385.6 without a body push, the height-fitted arm reached
#    z -0.55 and its 10% stretch ended before z -0.60; 385.9 pushes the body 4 units back looking ahead, which moves
#    that window nearer: measured there, stretch 0.08 at z -0.535): within the limit, so the hand is on the controller
#    (error < 0.5 units)
vr-sim hand right pos 0.2 -0.3 -0.535
@frames 20
@assert vr.body.right.custom.stretch gt 0
@assert vr.body.right.custom.stretch lt 0.1
@assert vr.body.right.custom.error lt 0.5
@shot fit-near-limit

# 4. A hand well within the reach: no stretch, the hand on the controller
vr-sim hand right pos 0.2 -0.3 -0.3
@frames 20
@assert vr.body.right.custom.stretch eq 0
@assert vr.body.right.custom.error lt 0.5

# 5. The elbow drop: the right hand holds the sword (mvp-items), the empty left hand does not
vr-sim hand left on
vr-sim hand left pos -0.2 -0.3 -0.35
vr-sim hand right pos 0.2 -0.3 -0.35
vr-sim hand right rot 0 90 0
vr-sim hand left rot 0 90 0
@frames 20
@assert vr.weapon.inHand eq true
@assert vr.body.right.custom.elbowDrop gt 0
@assert vr.body.left.custom.elbowDrop eq 0
@shot elbow-drop

# 6. The right controller lost and found again: the sword is back in the hand and the drop with it
vr-sim hand right off
@frames 10
vr-sim hand right on
@frames 20
@assert vr.body.right.custom.elbowDrop gt 0

@assert errors eq 0
